      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "βελτίων βέλτιον (βελτιον-) ‘better’ (comparative of ἀγαθός)\ns.\n  m.lf.\n  n.\nNom. βελτίων\n  βέλτιον\nAcc.\n  βελτίον-α or βελτίω\n  βέλτιον\nGen.\n  βελτίον-ος\n  βελτίον-ος\nDat.\n  βελτίον-ι\n  βελτίον-ι\npl.\n  m.lf.\n  n.\nNom. βελτίον-ες or βελτίους\n  βελτίον-α or βελτίω\nAcc.\n  βελτίον-ας or βελτίους*\n  βελτίον-α or βελτίω\nGen.\n  βελτίον-ων\n  βελτίον-ων\nDat.\n  βελτίοσι(ν)\n  βελτίοσι(ν)",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 3,
      "bbox": [
        [
          388,
          227,
          461,
          915
        ]
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Note the alternative forms in the m./f. acc. s. and the m./f./n. nom. and acc. pl.\nThese are old forms, arising from a stem ending not in -ιον- but in -ιο-:\nβελτίο(ν)α > βελτίω (m./f. acc. s.; n. nom./acc. pl.)\nβελτίο(ν)ες > βελτίους (m./f. nom. pl.)",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "footnote",
      "order": 4,
      "bbox": [
        [
          477,
          194,
          529,
          915
        ]
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "* This form, which should by contraction be βελτίως, has not in fact been contracted but simply\ntaken over from the nom. pl.\nYou will find that these old forms are used far more often by Greek authors than their new -ν- stem\nequivalents.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
